    "requirement_contract": "`specroad artifact update <ID>` MUSS RFC-6902-Patches sowie die Komfortoptionen `--set <JSON-POINTER>=<JSON-VALUE>` und `--unset <JSON-POINTER>` unterstützen und eine erwartete Revision oder einen erwarteten Hash verlangen.",
    "scope": "Pure RFC-6902 and guarded value previews plus actual embedding-service updates on a complete local Goal/Requirement model: explicit revision/hash, all six patch operations, ordered set/unset, one revision, live host authorization, no-op and native historical replay. No registered CLI, general production model loading, dry-run/stdout or platform completion claim. R extends native behavior evidence to original-target input ownership, approved-to-proposed revision, byte-preserving draft/proposed no-op, stale/controlled input refusal and partial-publication recovery preservation. The automatic native lifecycle gate is limited to this updated proposed subject; it is not an approval/history certificate or a general replacement for other required services."
  },
